right now election workers are  recounting votes in a razor thin race  for clark county commission district c  democrat and former secretary of state  ross miller beat republican  las vegas city council member stavros  anthony by just 10 votes in the november  election  our bianca holman is live at clark  county election headquarters with a  closer look at this process hi bianca  this will be one of the busiest days for  the recount election staff will be  recounting the in person  and early voting in-person ballots  throughout the day  now here's what happened anthony had a  lead election night but that lead was  gone when the mail-in ballots were  counted  eventually ross miller would win by just  10 votes  the county certified the vote last week  that's despite election officials saying  they identified 139 voting discrepancies  in the race  including some cases where people  possibly voted twice  for a while it looked like there would  be a complete re-vote in clark county  district c  but that didn't happen and the county  commission certified the totals  one reason this race is so closely  watched is not just because of the slim  vote margin  anthony is hoping to be the first  republican elected to the clark county  commission in  16 years joe gloria the clark county  registrar  says that everything was read in for the  general election  last month will be taken off the shelf  and counted again  we've got it counted exactly the same  way that we counted ballots  leading into the election the difference  is we don't have to wait for the county  board to do work  the ballots are basically prepped  because they've already been through the  county board process and been counted  one time  so we can move at a much brisker pace  now any candidate is able to call for a  recount which anthony did last week his  campaign says this recount effort will  cost 80 thousand dollars  gloria tells us the mail-in ballots will  be counted throughout the remainder  of this week and then we should have a  final report on friday  reporting from cheyenne mlk bia  oklahoman 8 news now
 

